    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "look i get that standard models won't see it. garch and autocorrelation only work if the data is contained within the price action itself. but what if the price action is just the *result* of the signal? the lag between the event and the market move is what i'm studying. \n\nit's not about \"random noise\" to me, it's about the lag. the 10:04am white sedan/L-train/Frankfurt sequence follows almost the exact same temporal delta that preceded the mid-2024 dip. if we assume these aren't coincidences but rather latent macro-signals that the institutional algos are actually fed on, how would you go about quantifying the delay between a physical event stimulus and a volatility spike? i just want to see if the timing intervals are consistent across different types of events.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
